{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/275098-gmc-synergist-project-and-online-24-7-role-play-chat-game","id":275098,"title":"GMC: Synergist Project and online 24/7 Role Play Chat game","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-07T18:58:16-07:00","id":275098,"title":"GMC: Synergist Project and online 24/7 Role Play Chat game","content":"Hello everyone.<br /> <br /> I might be new to posting, but not new to the online and gaming role play community. From being involved in STing various games in the past, and hosting my own chat, I've now begun a new gaming campaign at the online chat site that I admin and own named <a href=\"http://www.storysanctum.com\" target=\"_blank\">www.storysanctum.com</a> .<br /> <br /> If you are not familiar with a 24/7 role play chat experience, let me explain in brief. We use addonchat, and once you are sanctioned you use forums to create actions behind the scenes between you and your STs, but play in character on the chat for role play with players and ST interaction. It is, in my opinion, a way to get truly submersed in plot and characters to the fullest.<br /> <br /> At Storysanctum I am running a God Machine Chronicle that takes influences from such movies as Gattaca, The Island, and other futuristic Sci-Fi Utopian/Dystopian settings. Though the game is just over a month in, I would love to draw some more people to the site and the games being played there. Here's a small blurb on Synergist Project as taken from the website, though the game itself has already moved a little more from Utopia into the fact a lot of pc's are coming to realize not everything is as it seems, and darkness has its teeth sunk in to their society even if they do not know it. This takes a 'God Machine to the fullest' approach in which technology, the cog in the machine propels all existence. But what about when that machine starts to eliminate all it was built to protect?: <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><a href=\"http://storysanctum.com/wiki/index.php?title=File:PSYN.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"http://storysanctum.com/wiki/images/a/a0/PSYN.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a> </span></span></span></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#808080\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">\u203a <span style=\"font-family:Book Antiqua\">Setting</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Book Antiqua\"><i>\u201cWe are at heart so profoundly anarchistic that the only form of state we can imagine living in is Utopian; and so cynical that the only Utopia we can believe in is authoritarian.\u201d</i> \u2015 Lionel Trilling</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><i>A beautiful unblemished piece of perfection. That is all the people of Haven have ever known. White wash walls, pristine ivory spires, and vast marble thresholds. Haven is a Utopian society in which all are born inside her walls and know only of her existence. Those who inhabit her have been born, in their own respects, and raised among the many other Havenites which inhabit, build and propel her into the epitome of existence.</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><i>Haven has always been inhabited by its three primary races of humanoid species. The Homo-Primo, or First Born, are humans who carry the pure and blemished genetic make up of two First Born humans. At their core the First Born are as human as they come, and in Haven, the Primo come very degenerated in comparison to their biologically engineered cousins. The First Born, however faulted they may be, are also incredibly adaptable and there are rumors in Haven that some of them even dream of the past. For all of these reasons, in a society that would have no accounts of disorderly thinking, there is a stigma tied to being born Primo.</i></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><i>The Homo-Supernus, or Elite Born, are perfected specimens cultivated in laboratories and born of flawless genetic make up. The Elite are beautiful, hyper-intelligent, physically superior, and have superior control of their emotions and desires. Though the Primo might find them cold, calculating and dull, they are the backbone of Haven society. The Primo will die out eventually, but the Supernus? They will last forever, for they are the science and the blood that knows no end.</i></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><i>Lastly, and most rare, are the Homo-Hibrida, or more commonly, the Hybrids. Understanding what a Hybrid is, has always been a mystery that plagues the Primo's, while the Supernus are sure to never question their existence. The Hybrids are the something-other in Haven society that no one really talks about, but they certainly answer to them. They are the Chancellors, Leaders and Upper-most Class of Haven known as The Hierarchy. They do not descend among the lower levels of Havens Sectors to nurture those beneath them, but lead from an unknown distance. In Haven this is not questioned. In Haven this is simply what has always been...</i></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">If anyone has any questions at all, please feel free to hit me up in skype, come register at the chat and pop in to say hi, or post here! Thank you for your time. We'd love to see you come by!</span></span></span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4024,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4024-storysanctum","user":"storysanctum","date":". 10-07-2014, 10:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4024-storysanctum","name":"storysanctum","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4024_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}